  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready: six questions on O4, \"Workflows and agents: who owns the control flow?\" It's in `quizzes/0002.json`, and its key is in `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **Questions:** Five are multiple choice or numeric and one is a short answer. They use makerspace cases like booking, the manual lookup, and cost per request.\n- **What they cover:** Who owns the control flow, and when a fixed workflow beats an agent. That includes a routing case and a cost comparison tied to your model budget.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** There is no lesson on workflows versus agents yet, so this quiz is ahead of the lessons. It's a check of the objective itself. I wrote it from my own knowledge and didn't search for a source, so nothing here is cited.\n- **What it assumes:** Only the agent loop from quiz 0001. I'd suggest a short lesson on this objective first if the ideas are new to you.\n- **Misconceptions:** I left the `distractors` field out of the key. The only misconception ids in the workspace are M1, M3, M4 and M6, and I couldn't tell what M1, M3 and M6 mean. So I explained each wrong answer in the rationale instead.\n\nWant to take it here in the chat, or have a lesson first?",
